==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*4 [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*6 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Puffzerker]] spawns as the boss after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is recommended to collect all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]] Chapter 1, 2, & 3, otherwise Hyppoh will become a mild inconvenience. Additionally, if you possess [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], he is an infinitely superior pick to [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Ranger]] despite the latter's [[Cat Combo]].

Let the Cat Base tank and immediately save up for [[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Prime DX]], who nukes the peons and cripples Hyppoh. By this point Puffzerker and Capy will spawn; you want at least three meatshields to ensure that Giga-Nyan isn't sniped by Capy. It's just a waiting game now, slowly chipping the Red enemies with Blue Nyanko Ranger and Giga-Nyan until you're able to get out a second Giga-Nyan. [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] and/or [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] help control Capy, making them excellent picks for assurance in case things go wrong. Killing either one of the Capies or Puffzerker usually means victory, since the other two supports lose immense pushing power as a result. Make sure to bring [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] (or any other expendable DPS like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]) for extra DPS against Hyppoh and Shibalien.

